1
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:13,303
TOKYO

2
00:00:13,399 --> 00:00:16,909
Simultaneous kidnappings
have struck seven cities in Asia!

3
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,562
Not just Seoul.

4
00:00:20,159 --> 00:00:24,259
People were kidnapped
in other Asian cities at the same time.

5
00:00:25,284 --> 00:00:28,623
In Singapore, a man was
abducted in a restaurant.

6
00:00:29,576 --> 00:00:33,256
In Bangkok, a woman was
apparently taken from her home.

7
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:38,428
In Manila, a woman aged 20 was
seized on her way home from work.

8
00:00:39,743 --> 00:00:44,201
In Taipei, a man was abducted
in front of his teenage daughter.

9
00:00:45,659 --> 00:00:47,909
There was also a case in Naha.

10
00:00:53,409 --> 00:00:55,201
SAORI
KIDNAP GAME

11
00:00:55,284 --> 00:00:57,284
"kiDnap GAME"?

12
00:00:57,618 --> 00:01:01,743
"Only one shall prevail...
Only one shall survive..."

13
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,580
MISSION

14
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:13,039
CAPTURE THE MASTERMIND.

15
00:01:14,247 --> 00:01:17,080
Capture the mastermind...

16
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:03,580
KIDNAP GAME

17
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,902
39 HOURS UNTIL THE FIRST CASUALTY OF
KIDNAP GAME

18
00:02:11,137 --> 00:02:14,220
SINGAPORE
DAY 1

19
00:02:14,637 --> 00:02:17,553
Sir, I've just got this text!

20
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:18,970
PM 07:00 SGT

21
00:02:19,877 --> 00:02:21,335
"kiDnap GAME?"

22
00:02:21,591 --> 00:02:24,209
It must be from the kidnapper.
Tony was kidnapped.

23
00:02:25,303 --> 00:02:28,595
It says “Clear the checkpoints
within the time limits and reach the goal.

24
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:32,720
"Checkpoint One: The treasure-laden ship founders.
Time limit: forty-four hours."

25
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:39,137
Maybe you're famous enough to attract
this kind of malicious prank.

26
00:02:39,762 --> 00:02:42,220
What do you mean? It’s not a prank!

27
00:02:42,345 --> 00:02:44,043
Tony will die if I don’t complete this mission.

28
00:02:44,095 --> 00:02:45,428
You’re already breaking this rule, though.

29
00:02:45,637 --> 00:02:49,220
It says “Do not notify or request assistance
from state authorities,”

30
00:02:49,338 --> 00:02:50,490
but that’s us.

31
00:02:55,387 --> 00:02:56,350
Yeah.

32
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:00,723
Yeah, it's a prank.

33
00:03:02,927 --> 00:03:05,650
You know, forget I mentioned it,
it’s definitely a prank.

34
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:13,845
TOKYO
DAY 1

35
00:03:15,387 --> 00:03:19,012
PM 08:02 JST

36
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,762
DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE
FROM STATE AUTHORITIES.

37
00:03:26,845 --> 00:03:28,303
RULE-BREAKERS WILL BE DISQUALIFIED.

38
00:03:29,928 --> 00:03:30,928
Niide? You okay?

39
00:03:31,512 --> 00:03:34,095
Yeah. Did you find anything out?

40
00:03:35,053 --> 00:03:39,012
We can't track the vehicle
or locate her phone.

41
00:03:39,137 --> 00:03:42,803
What about witnesses?!
There's got to be something!

42
00:03:42,887 --> 00:03:44,345
-But, um...
-Move.

43
00:03:44,428 --> 00:03:45,595
Where are you going?

44
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:49,262
Hold it, Niide! Think about what's happening.

45
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:53,320
Simultaneous abductions in seven cities.

46
00:03:53,445 --> 00:03:55,362
We don't know their demands.

47
00:03:55,387 --> 00:03:56,670
They demand...

48
00:03:57,178 --> 00:03:59,512
“DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE
FROM STATE AUTHORITIES.

49
00:03:59,637 --> 00:04:01,928
RULE-BREAKERS WILL BE DISQUALIFIED.

50
00:04:03,095 --> 00:04:04,512
They demand...

51
00:04:09,678 --> 00:04:11,803
SHINJUKU CENTRAL POLICE STATION

52
00:04:11,887 --> 00:04:13,262
AM 09:12 JST

53
00:04:13,345 --> 00:04:14,512
NOTICE OF LEAVE

54
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,381
What the hell is this?

55
00:04:18,063 --> 00:04:19,480
You need to stay home.

56
00:04:19,563 --> 00:04:21,563
What's the meaning of this?

57
00:04:24,688 --> 00:04:26,480
KIDNAPPING VICTIMS NAMED

58
00:04:26,563 --> 00:04:28,476
SAORI NIIDE
TOMIKO HIGA

59
00:04:28,563 --> 00:04:33,230
Why is Saori's name in the news?
Someone here is leaking info!

60
00:04:33,313 --> 00:04:34,896
That's not possible...

61
00:04:35,473 --> 00:04:36,772
I can't trust anyone.

62
00:04:37,998 --> 00:04:40,235
I'll save her myself.

63
00:04:40,681 --> 00:04:44,181
What can you do alone?
The SIT suspects you!

64
00:04:44,264 --> 00:04:46,181
They're way off mark!

65
00:04:46,264 --> 00:04:48,598
Expect to be watched.

66
00:04:48,880 --> 00:04:52,050
We can't help you either.
You've got no allies.

67
00:04:53,829 --> 00:04:55,023
I know.

68
00:04:59,786 --> 00:05:01,453
Where are you going?

69
00:05:01,538 --> 00:05:03,496
This is a grudge against me.

70
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,455
Have you got a lead?!

71
00:05:05,505 --> 00:05:06,850
Out of the way!

72
00:05:06,968 --> 00:05:09,593
We received a tip regarding Saori!

73
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:16,710
A food vendor at the hospital
kept seeing a suspicious van.

74
00:05:17,569 --> 00:05:18,536
A suspicious van?

75
00:05:20,295 --> 00:05:21,462
Here.

76
00:05:21,706 --> 00:05:23,248
FLORIST'S VAN, ROSE LOGO
HOSPITAL

77
00:05:23,508 --> 00:05:24,633
Thanks.

78
00:05:27,547 --> 00:05:29,119
-That's him.
-Let's go.

79
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,193
Heading out.

80
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:49,903
Sorry! I'll be open in about ten minutes.

81
00:05:50,588 --> 00:05:53,256
I'm Niide, from Shinjuku Central Police.

82
00:05:55,297 --> 00:05:56,243
Are you Saori's...?

83
00:05:56,922 --> 00:05:57,880
Yes.

84
00:05:59,172 --> 00:06:03,172
I heard you saw
a suspicious florist's van.

85
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:04,422
Yes.

86
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:10,463
It parked over there every day
for about a week.

87
00:06:11,005 --> 00:06:12,523
It was there yesterday, too.

88
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,255
And the driver?

89
00:06:15,172 --> 00:06:16,755
I couldn't see inside.

90
00:06:17,338 --> 00:06:19,172
Anything else suspicious?

91
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,123
Not particularly.

92
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,063
I see.

93
00:06:29,838 --> 00:06:33,005
Do you not like carrots, by any chance?

94
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:35,505
No.

95
00:06:35,563 --> 00:06:40,271
Saori asked me about carrot recipes
more than once.

96
00:06:41,505 --> 00:06:44,338
I figured it was for someone special.

97
00:06:46,899 --> 00:06:47,556
Um...

98
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:51,922
This is my phone number.

99
00:06:52,713 --> 00:06:56,350
Please call me
if you remember anything else.

100
00:06:57,005 --> 00:06:58,047
Okay.

101
00:07:31,838 --> 00:07:32,672
How is it?

102
00:07:33,505 --> 00:07:35,755
Delicious.

103
00:07:36,797 --> 00:07:39,088
Eat a lot. It'll cure your temper.

104
00:07:40,255 --> 00:07:44,213
Beta-carotene doesn't have that effect,
does it?

105
00:07:46,130 --> 00:07:49,963
It does if you think so.
Trust me, I'm a nurse.

106
00:07:51,213 --> 00:07:52,255
I trust you.

107
00:07:53,172 --> 00:07:54,213
Seconds, then?

108
00:07:54,797 --> 00:07:57,505
-What?! Wait...
-No ifs, no buts.

109
00:08:14,683 --> 00:08:18,433
How do you know the missing nurse?

110
00:08:20,572 --> 00:08:23,896
I met her when I was hospitalized
and became friends.

111
00:08:26,503 --> 00:08:28,884
So you can talk to her husband...

112
00:08:29,883 --> 00:08:32,876
I can't push an interview on him now.

113
00:08:34,756 --> 00:08:37,169
This is a chance to redeem yourself.

114
00:08:43,338 --> 00:08:44,255
Excuse me.

115
00:08:46,078 --> 00:08:47,286
Hello?

116
00:08:48,187 --> 00:08:49,853
I need a favor.

117
00:08:51,230 --> 00:08:53,522
Get me info on the other hostages.

118
00:08:53,963 --> 00:08:55,297
Why me?

119
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:58,838
I can't rely on the police. I'm a suspect.

120
00:09:00,917 --> 00:09:03,917
A regular investigation won't cut it.

121
00:09:04,251 --> 00:09:08,792
I need a different approach.
And I need your help for that.

122
00:09:11,088 --> 00:09:11,963
All right.

123
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:13,880
Thanks.

124
00:09:23,047 --> 00:09:24,213
Crap.

125
00:09:38,005 --> 00:09:40,047
-Where is he?
-He got away.

126
00:09:40,172 --> 00:09:41,463
Dammit.

127
00:09:43,005 --> 00:09:45,297
These are the other hostages.

128
00:09:45,838 --> 00:09:47,255
Thanks.

129
00:09:48,063 --> 00:09:50,147
With this doctor's daughter,

130
00:09:50,254 --> 00:09:54,504
and this IT CEO's mother,
the motive could be ransom.

131
00:09:55,297 --> 00:09:59,047
The man in Taipei
is married to a famous model.

132
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,136
The Bangkok woman's family is rich.

133
00:10:04,236 --> 00:10:08,270
But this girl in Manila
comes from a poor family,

134
00:10:09,115 --> 00:10:13,865
and her grandfather even had to work
in Japan as a delivery driver.

135
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:19,922
If the objective isn't money,
what could it be...?

136
00:10:20,935 --> 00:10:24,310
Some kind of revenge, or grudge...

137
00:10:25,366 --> 00:10:28,075
Who could hold a grudge against Saori?

138
00:10:29,098 --> 00:10:33,890
The grudge is probably against me.
Saori's just caught up in this.

139
00:10:35,705 --> 00:10:37,330
If that's the case,

140
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:41,372
could the same person
resent these people, too?

141
00:10:42,225 --> 00:10:43,142
No way.

142
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:45,537
I guess not.

143
00:10:45,562 --> 00:10:51,310
If it's not about money or revenge,
and the victims were chosen at random...

144
00:10:52,919 --> 00:10:56,503
Is it just to make headlines
or for the fun of it?

145
00:11:00,271 --> 00:11:01,896
Did you think of something?

146
00:11:03,255 --> 00:11:04,547
No...

147
00:11:07,763 --> 00:11:12,047
If the criminal's a thrill-seeker
who wants to make headlines,

148
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:14,243
you won't be able to stop him alone.

149
00:11:15,083 --> 00:11:18,005
I'm gonna hunt the bastard down.

150
00:11:19,032 --> 00:11:21,763
That attitude is what pained Saori.

151
00:11:21,794 --> 00:11:23,163
Then what am I supposed to do?

152
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:26,383
You need to stay level-headed.

153
00:11:31,015 --> 00:11:32,136
What do you plan to do?

154
00:11:35,349 --> 00:11:38,230
I met a strange man the night before last.

155
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,936
I'll investigate him.

156
00:11:43,664 --> 00:11:47,085
PM 05:03 JST

157
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,253
Akina?

158
00:11:54,337 --> 00:11:57,712
Hey, you know anything about
the "kiDnap GAME"?

159
00:12:00,710 --> 00:12:04,550
The girlfriend of the victim in Singapore
is an influencer,

160
00:12:05,376 --> 00:12:08,710
and she made a post
about this "kiDnap GAME" thing.

161
00:12:09,002 --> 00:12:11,002
It's kinda gone viral.

162
00:12:11,251 --> 00:12:15,543
ANYONE HEARD OF THE KIDNAP GAME?

163
00:12:19,803 --> 00:12:22,469
-Sorry.
-It's okay.

164
00:12:29,835 --> 00:12:32,710
Oh, no. Oh no, wait, wait...

165
00:12:33,751 --> 00:12:35,168
You never heard of it?

166
00:12:37,626 --> 00:12:40,626
Never.

167
00:12:41,085 --> 00:12:42,251
Oh well.

168
00:12:42,918 --> 00:12:46,751
I thought it was worth mentioning.
I'll keep digging.

169
00:12:46,918 --> 00:12:48,960
Okay, thanks.

170
00:12:56,157 --> 00:12:59,616
PM 09:45 JST

171
00:13:24,772 --> 00:13:25,897
Toyoda.

172
00:13:26,334 --> 00:13:27,251
Niide?

173
00:13:27,335 --> 00:13:29,169
I need to see some footage.

174
00:13:30,178 --> 00:13:34,282
Is this about your wife's case?
I can't authorize that.

175
00:13:34,491 --> 00:13:36,032
Her trail's gone cold.

176
00:13:36,116 --> 00:13:37,616
It's a different person.

177
00:13:38,574 --> 00:13:42,491
Please. Saori's life depends on it.

178
00:13:48,116 --> 00:13:51,449
My shift ends in ten minutes.
We need to hurry.

179
00:13:51,532 --> 00:13:52,407
Thanks.

180
00:13:54,077 --> 00:13:59,202
Tokyo Metro Tocho Nishimae Station,
night before last, 11 PM.

181
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:27,616
That's him.

182
00:14:27,907 --> 00:14:30,449
I'll track him with face recognition.

183
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:55,336
That's the place? Thanks.

184
00:14:56,616 --> 00:14:59,782
PM 11:54 JST

185
00:17:08,616 --> 00:17:11,199
Saori! Saori!

186
00:17:16,491 --> 00:17:23,290
I'M NOT THE ONE YOU'RE AFTER!
THE GAME GOES ON!

187
00:17:38,393 --> 00:17:39,496
Dammit!

188
00:17:54,394 --> 00:17:57,935
"BAR NEON LIGHT," KABUKICHO,
NOON TOMORROW.

189
00:18:18,851 --> 00:18:21,309
Why are you doing this?

190
00:18:25,309 --> 00:18:28,810
My husband is a detective.
He'll come for me, just you wait.

191
00:18:30,892 --> 00:18:32,767
He'll come for me!

192
00:18:36,226 --> 00:18:38,809
SEOUL
DAY 1

193
00:18:38,892 --> 00:18:40,559
PM 08:00 KST

194
00:18:44,767 --> 00:18:47,434
MISSION

195
00:18:55,184 --> 00:18:56,351
Kiju?!

196
00:18:59,267 --> 00:18:59,976
Ayun.

197
00:19:00,001 --> 00:19:03,250
Where's Rian? Where?

198
00:19:03,931 --> 00:19:09,596
It's my fault. I took my eyes off her.

199
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:14,029
Why would you do that?!

200
00:19:14,615 --> 00:19:17,574
Rian can't see anything!

201
00:19:29,101 --> 00:19:32,642
AM 10:12 KST

202
00:19:47,226 --> 00:19:51,601
KO WOON-MUK

203
00:20:24,476 --> 00:20:26,892
THIS COMPLETES MY MISSION, DOES IT NOT?

204
00:20:36,559 --> 00:20:40,017
GAME RULES VIOLATED. YOU ARE DISQUALIFIED.

205
00:20:43,892 --> 00:20:46,559
No, no, no!

206
00:20:48,684 --> 00:20:51,934
I APOLOGIZE. PLEASE DON’T HURT RIAN.

207
00:21:16,434 --> 00:21:20,193
ONE MORE FALSE REPORT AND
YOUR DAUGHTER DIES.

208
00:21:32,359 --> 00:21:34,025
Are you okay, Dr. Han?

209
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:46,874
My deepest sympathies.
Is there any way I can help?

210
00:21:51,547 --> 00:21:52,810
Will you be needing a body?

211
00:21:57,553 --> 00:21:58,489
What do you mean?

212
00:21:59,516 --> 00:22:01,950
I can take care of unsavory work.

213
00:22:09,018 --> 00:22:13,518
It was you, was it?
Where were you last night?

214
00:22:14,437 --> 00:22:16,490
Did you send me that bogus text?

215
00:22:18,576 --> 00:22:21,226
People are watching, Doctor.

216
00:22:53,857 --> 00:22:56,107
MISSION

217
00:22:56,232 --> 00:23:00,107
COMMIT MURDER.

218
00:23:08,288 --> 00:23:11,690
PM 02:22 KST

219
00:23:12,899 --> 00:23:14,524
But it's too far.

220
00:23:14,607 --> 00:23:16,565
It's possible.

221
00:23:42,815 --> 00:23:45,440
MISSION
COMMIT MURDER.

222
00:23:50,788 --> 00:23:51,830
Where were you?

223
00:24:05,940 --> 00:24:07,982
Why Rian?

224
00:24:10,897 --> 00:24:13,553
She's not someone people would resent...

225
00:24:15,390 --> 00:24:20,643
If anyone's resented, it's us.
We're living in too much luxury...

226
00:24:21,722 --> 00:24:26,819
We're hated and resented!

227
00:24:29,386 --> 00:24:30,423
Maybe.

228
00:24:34,783 --> 00:24:40,556
Get her back!
I don't care about this lifestyle...

229
00:24:42,806 --> 00:24:44,950
I only need Rian!

230
00:24:48,211 --> 00:24:49,086
Come here.

231
00:24:52,743 --> 00:24:54,429
I feel the same way.

232
00:24:56,989 --> 00:24:58,909
Do you really?

233
00:25:00,266 --> 00:25:02,795
Five years ago, you could have saved her.

234
00:25:05,625 --> 00:25:07,667
You took the light from her.

235
00:25:17,257 --> 00:25:19,465
PM 11:45 KST

236
00:25:19,632 --> 00:25:24,632
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

237
00:25:58,424 --> 00:26:01,174
COMMIT MURDER.

238
00:26:05,632 --> 00:26:07,299
Kill me...

239
00:26:09,507 --> 00:26:14,590
Put me out of my misery...

240
00:26:25,843 --> 00:26:27,218
Dr. Han?

241
00:26:29,007 --> 00:26:29,976
Looking for something?

242
00:26:30,602 --> 00:26:34,116
No, it's fine.

243
00:26:36,795 --> 00:26:37,736
Dr. Han.

244
00:26:40,523 --> 00:26:44,843
Were you asking today about
where Mr. Park, the undertaker,

245
00:26:45,117 --> 00:26:47,696
was last night?

246
00:26:50,070 --> 00:26:54,576
He was at the hospital
shortly before you phoned us.

247
00:26:55,612 --> 00:26:58,170
I was wondering what he was doing...

248
00:27:03,653 --> 00:27:10,076
Someone help me... Dad... Mom...

249
00:27:14,416 --> 00:27:18,862
MANILA
DAY 1

250
00:27:26,817 --> 00:27:31,217
It’s your birthday soon, right Lolo?
Anything you want?

251
00:27:32,403 --> 00:27:36,987
No it's okay. Don’t worry,
I’ve been saving up money just like you...

252
00:27:37,112 --> 00:27:39,945
Yeah. So what do you want?

253
00:27:40,070 --> 00:27:43,243
Clothes? Shoes? Or...

254
00:27:43,742 --> 00:27:44,781
No! No!

255
00:27:45,029 --> 00:27:48,237
Maria! Maria, what’s happening?!

256
00:27:54,153 --> 00:27:56,195
MISSION

257
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:59,903
PREPARE 10 MILLION PESOS IN CASH.

258
00:28:05,445 --> 00:28:06,612
Maria...

259
00:28:09,987 --> 00:28:13,445
AM 07:22 PHT

260
00:28:18,778 --> 00:28:20,445
I'm back!

261
00:28:21,096 --> 00:28:22,376
Maria!

262
00:28:23,987 --> 00:28:27,653
Here, pocket money.

263
00:28:28,482 --> 00:28:30,857
All this? Are you sure?

264
00:28:32,161 --> 00:28:35,453
Dad, you shouldn’t give her money
every time just like that.

265
00:28:35,945 --> 00:28:39,362
I got a big tip from a rich tourist today.

266
00:28:39,487 --> 00:28:44,503
It’s because you’re the best!
Thank you!

267
00:28:56,945 --> 00:29:01,903
Dad, You conned that money
from those tourists, didn’t you?

268
00:29:05,112 --> 00:29:10,528
You’ve got to stop that, Dad.
Life isn’t all about money.

269
00:29:12,533 --> 00:29:16,366
You only say that because
you haven't been poor.

270
00:29:19,278 --> 00:29:23,487
People who chase money
get what’s coming to them.

271
00:29:27,403 --> 00:29:29,278
Nothing comes.

272
00:29:30,869 --> 00:29:34,849
There’s no God, no Buddha to punish anyone.

273
00:29:36,196 --> 00:29:39,779
I’m done with the shame of begging,

274
00:29:41,136 --> 00:29:44,695
done with being worked
to the bone in a foreign country.

275
00:29:45,820 --> 00:29:49,945
You think I can let my daughter
and granddaughter go through that?!

276
00:30:05,076 --> 00:30:07,451
Please! Sir! Wait!

277
00:30:07,493 --> 00:30:11,922
Miguel, you’re a great employee and
a great friend, but you’ll make a terrible debtor.

278
00:30:13,149 --> 00:30:16,636
-Why?
-You’re too old to pay it back.

279
00:30:17,416 --> 00:30:21,749
But sir, I’ll do anything!
I'll work day and night for the rest of my life...

280
00:30:21,810 --> 00:30:25,596
That’s how accidents happen.
I won’t let you do that.

281
00:30:26,845 --> 00:30:28,143
That’s all I have to say.

282
00:31:15,737 --> 00:31:17,278
Hi, sir. Good morning.

283
00:31:22,461 --> 00:31:23,689
Cash me in.

284
00:31:29,335 --> 00:31:30,699
All in on 12.

285
00:31:32,403 --> 00:31:33,778
Are you sure, sir?

286
00:31:36,320 --> 00:31:37,320
Yes.

287
00:32:16,132 --> 00:32:18,299
Wait, wait! One more time.

288
00:32:18,632 --> 00:32:21,965
One more time.
Please, give me another chance!

289
00:32:22,090 --> 00:32:25,143
-Excuse me, sir. Was there a problem here?
-One more time!

290
00:32:25,174 --> 00:32:28,176
-Sorry, you have to go!
-Please! Maria’s life depends on it!

291
00:32:28,216 --> 00:32:33,091
Please! Maria’s life depends on it!
Wait! No, no, no...

292
00:32:33,780 --> 00:32:36,853
Please wait! Give me one more chance!

293
00:32:40,006 --> 00:32:40,860
Please don't come back!

294
00:32:42,905 --> 00:32:44,956
-Please!
-Stop it!

295
00:32:52,340 --> 00:32:53,516
“kiDnap GAME”?

296
00:32:54,856 --> 00:32:55,924
This.

297
00:32:59,003 --> 00:33:01,048
Could be a prank, but if not...

298
00:33:02,170 --> 00:33:04,063
“Only one shall survive”!

299
00:33:06,183 --> 00:33:09,730
If we do not collect the ten million pesos
before the others,

300
00:33:11,458 --> 00:33:14,169
then Maria gets killed! Do you get that?!

301
00:33:17,389 --> 00:33:19,463
We need to get the money right away!

302
00:33:24,892 --> 00:33:26,267
I know where to get the money.

303
00:33:27,992 --> 00:33:29,158
Where?

304
00:33:32,132 --> 00:33:33,715
The bank.

305
00:33:35,590 --> 00:33:36,507
What?

306
00:33:37,965 --> 00:33:40,382
We'll get the money from the bank I work at.

307
00:33:41,911 --> 00:33:44,286
I know how the bank operates.

308
00:33:45,816 --> 00:33:48,715
Most bank robberies fail. How can this work?

309
00:33:49,007 --> 00:33:53,049
We just need to hand over the money, right?

310
00:33:56,378 --> 00:33:57,596
I get it.

311
00:33:59,465 --> 00:34:01,757
I don’t care if I get caught.

312
00:34:03,345 --> 00:34:07,386
As long as we get the money,
we can save Maria!

313
00:34:07,507 --> 00:34:11,299
Right. we're fine even if you get caught.

314
00:34:11,762 --> 00:34:13,736
It doesn't matter if I get caught.

315
00:34:16,924 --> 00:34:18,924
I don't care if I die.

316
00:34:20,621 --> 00:34:23,204
As long as Maria’s safe!

317
00:34:29,715 --> 00:34:36,196
Help me. Please save me. Please let me out.
I'm begging you. Please help!

318
00:34:43,608 --> 00:34:46,692
KIDNAP GAME
DAY 2

319
00:34:48,257 --> 00:34:51,465
AM 07:49 PHT

320
00:34:54,295 --> 00:34:57,154
Good morning, sir.

321
00:34:58,996 --> 00:35:03,090
-I’m very sorry about yesterday.
-That’s fine, forget it.

322
00:35:04,330 --> 00:35:07,965
Oh, you’ve got a flat tire.

323
00:35:08,470 --> 00:35:10,965
Right before an important meeting.

324
00:35:12,421 --> 00:35:16,229
I can take you, if you like.
By way of apology.

325
00:35:16,696 --> 00:35:17,882
That would be good.

326
00:35:35,913 --> 00:35:37,246
I hope you didn’t kill him.

327
00:35:37,724 --> 00:35:39,724
He’s fine. More importantly...

328
00:36:10,688 --> 00:36:16,041
I would like to deposit a company deed.
I’m acting as an agent.

329
00:36:16,965 --> 00:36:18,132
Ma'am.

330
00:36:24,007 --> 00:36:26,215
ENTRANCE

331
00:36:34,618 --> 00:36:38,650
-Hey Ricky. Cash truck is arriving.
-OK.

332
00:36:49,036 --> 00:36:54,883
May I see some kind of IDs to confirm
your and the principal’s names and addresses?

333
00:37:02,037 --> 00:37:03,117
Oh, thank you.

334
00:37:14,806 --> 00:37:15,973
Thank you.

335
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:33,698
Sorry for keeping you waiting, sir.

336
00:37:34,547 --> 00:37:35,520
This way, please.

337
00:37:44,182 --> 00:37:47,890
KABUKICHO FIRST AVENUE

338
00:38:03,062 --> 00:38:04,645
Welcome.

339
00:38:11,105 --> 00:38:12,397
You made it.

340
00:38:13,118 --> 00:38:17,490
The fact that you're here
means that you destroyed our dummy.

341
00:38:18,089 --> 00:38:19,464
So predictable.

342
00:38:19,781 --> 00:38:22,740
Don't touch me if you care about your wife.

343
00:38:22,906 --> 00:38:24,240
Where is she?!

344
00:38:27,179 --> 00:38:28,679
On the track.

345
00:38:30,198 --> 00:38:31,303
Did you text me?

346
00:38:31,883 --> 00:38:34,196
You mean about the game?

347
00:38:35,823 --> 00:38:39,406
I'm not playing around. People could die.

348
00:38:40,740 --> 00:38:46,115
-May I help you carry your bag, sir?
-No no, it's OK.

349
00:38:55,490 --> 00:38:58,115
-You may come in, sir.
-Thank you.

350
00:39:05,865 --> 00:39:11,031
Oh, sorry. I left my key at the desk.

351
00:39:11,323 --> 00:39:14,365
No problem, sir. I'll just get it for you.

352
00:39:15,165 --> 00:39:15,998
Thank you.

353
00:39:48,193 --> 00:39:49,109
Are you okay, sir?

354
00:39:52,615 --> 00:39:54,740
Hey! Stop! Come back!

355
00:39:54,865 --> 00:39:58,448
Emergency!
The guard took a case of money!

356
00:40:00,573 --> 00:40:01,823
He’s on the run! Stop him!

357
00:40:12,615 --> 00:40:13,531
Stop!

358
00:40:18,281 --> 00:40:22,740
Stop! Freeze!

359
00:40:23,365 --> 00:40:24,490
Stop!

360
00:40:28,173 --> 00:40:32,983
No! Please no! I need that money.
My daughter’s been kidnapped. Please!

361
00:40:33,573 --> 00:40:35,240
I'll tell you something.

362
00:40:36,003 --> 00:40:39,365
One player's almost completed his mission.

363
00:40:42,084 --> 00:40:45,736
He's risking everything
to raise a king's ransom.

364
00:40:48,490 --> 00:40:52,115
The man in Manila? That's his mission?

365
00:40:52,948 --> 00:40:54,448
So whatcha gonna do?

366
00:40:57,281 --> 00:40:59,031
There's nothing you can do.

367
00:41:18,740 --> 00:41:20,115
What's going on?

368
00:41:23,448 --> 00:41:25,115
Where is the money, Ricky?

369
00:41:28,948 --> 00:41:30,031
No way...

370
00:41:53,823 --> 00:41:55,156
Excuse me, sir.

371
00:42:56,323 --> 00:42:59,589
Throw away your guns!
Throw away your guns!

372
00:43:02,653 --> 00:43:04,695
You! You!

373
00:43:06,490 --> 00:43:11,436
Put the money... all the money!
All the money, now!

374
00:43:16,103 --> 00:43:18,615
Give it to me! Give it to me!

375
00:43:52,548 --> 00:43:55,588
Stop the car!

376
00:43:56,108 --> 00:43:58,728
Get out of the car!

377
00:44:15,443 --> 00:44:20,781
Get out of the car! Now! Hands up!

378
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:39,876
Oh, God no!

379
00:44:41,992 --> 00:44:44,200
Please.

380
00:44:50,676 --> 00:44:54,906
Maria, Maria...

381
00:44:58,516 --> 00:45:02,423
Maria, Maria...!

382
00:45:35,563 --> 00:45:37,636
Read it. I'm not going to run.

383
00:45:52,592 --> 00:45:54,092
It's a game!

384
00:45:54,448 --> 00:45:58,686
It's a game! Maria's going to die. Please!

385
00:46:01,208 --> 00:46:05,182
We're not playing around. People could die.

386
00:46:08,198 --> 00:46:11,281
PLAYERS DEEMED INCAPABLE OF COMPLETING
THEIR MISSION WILL BE IMMEDIATELY DISQUALIFIED.

387
00:47:21,176 --> 00:47:22,259
Mama?

388
00:47:23,563 --> 00:47:24,636
Are you okay?

389
00:47:27,771 --> 00:47:28,249
Yeah...

390
00:47:50,146 --> 00:47:54,438
Hey, you haven't told anyone
about us, have you?

391
00:48:10,077 --> 00:48:11,286
Is it real?

392
00:48:12,936 --> 00:48:14,450
It’s actually for real...?

393
00:48:16,359 --> 00:48:19,389
Oh no... I’m running out of time...

394
00:48:20,462 --> 00:48:22,379
“The treasure-laden ship founders”?

395
00:48:23,188 --> 00:48:25,271
What’s that meant to mean?!

396
00:48:32,438 --> 00:48:35,730
TANG SHIPWRECK

397
00:48:35,855 --> 00:48:38,480
CHINESE TREASURES FROM THE 9TH CENTURY...

398
00:48:39,188 --> 00:48:41,980
This must be it!

399
00:48:44,771 --> 00:48:46,230
Why?

400
00:48:50,855 --> 00:48:53,313
Why are you doing this to us?

401
00:49:13,368 --> 00:49:16,063
KIDNAP GAME
CO-PRODUCTION PARTNERSHIP

402
00:49:16,146 --> 00:49:17,521
FUJI TELEVISION
MAKERVILLE SIMSTORY

403
00:49:17,646 --> 00:49:21,648
BASED ON KIDNAP GAME
CREATED BY YUSUKE KATO
